    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Oh, Daniel... This is a very, **very** big pain point for me right now. At the moment I am trying to force myself into writing at least basic tests for all of my modules. For some reason, I don't really like the current state of testing capabilities in \"Neovim Lua Plugin\" area. Can't quite grasp the exact thing here though (something along the lines of \"no single *straightforward* way\" and \"unnecessarily complex\").\r\n\r\nWell, that said, I am very close to accepting that 'plenary.test_harness' is as close as it might get to simplifying the process while getting reasonably wide range of capabilities.\r\n\r\nAlso, I am very open to creating 'mini.testing' and would really like to hear your thoughts on what it should look like to be useful for you.",
