        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Yeah, I find it somehow bizarre, I don't quite get it.\r\nCurrently, I use the busted api that plenary provides.\r\n\r\nI started to learn rust, and I liked the way rust finds test functions: https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/testing/unit_testing.html\r\n\r\nHaving this feature is somehow simpler that a whole test suite:\r\n- Just find an annotation (like `---@test Test name`) before a function\r\n- Provide some asserts, like assert equals, assert assert not equals\r\n- Create a mini.test function (like mini.doc scoping mechanism) to find all test functions, and run them",
            "created_at": "2022-02-23T09:04:08Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/47#issuecomment-1048570116",
