        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Ok, so is this more for \"find and run\" tests and not for writing them? Because there are at least these questions:\r\n- What is \"run test file\"? In which Neovim instance, under what environment, with what dependencies?\r\n- Having `before_each` and `after_each`, as well as mocks and stubs seems to be really useful. Should they also be a part of a possible module?\r\n- Should this also implement functionality for providing feedback about which tests failed and for what reason?",
